{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J4"],
      "pins": ["J4.1", "J4.2", "J4.3"],
      "nets": ["BAT+", "BAT-"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the barrel jack J4 has pin 1 (center) and pin 2 (sleeve) both wired onto the BAT+ node (the same vertical rail that carries J3 VBUS, C12 and IC1 VIN/EN), while pin 3 is wired to BAT-. The in-sheet note states '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug', so with no DC adapter inserted the internal contact directly shorts BAT+ to BAT-.",
      "expected": "The specification's corrected netlist requires J4.1->BAT+, J4.2->GND (sleeve), J4.3->BAT-, so that the normally-closed 2-3 contact ties BAT- to GND (closing the battery return) instead of shorting the cell. The spec even cites the historical fix commit ('now with power switch...') for exactly this wiring.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EthernetAndPower sheet, J4: text note '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug / 1 is center, center is positive'; pin 1 and pin 2 wires both join the BAT+ rail, pin 3 joins BAT-"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Netlist: J4.1->BAT+ (center/positive), J4.2->GND (sleeve), J4.3->BAT- ... a1d9676 'Meshinger 1.0 rev B WARNING THE DC PLUG PINS ARE WRONG, SHORTS BATTERY!'"}
      ],
      "impact": "Reproduces the documented rev-B 'SHORTS BATTERY' fault: with no plug the cell is shorted through the jack's internal switch; with a plug inserted the adapter sleeve (pin 2, tied to BAT+) is shorted to the adapter center (pin 1, also BAT+), shorting the external supply. This can damage the 18650 cell, U6 and the FAN53610 regulator and prevents the intended battery-disconnect function.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet C1, sitting from the Display_Power_Switch rail to GND in parallel with C2, is marked '0.1uF/16V'.",
      "expected": "The specification's component table lists schematic C1 as 1 uF / 25 V (the PDI 'C2 default' value, mapped to C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver sheet: 'C1 0.1uF/16V' on the Display_Power_Switch node"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 uF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 uF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD boost-converter input rail loses its intended 1 uF/25 V bulk/decoupling capacitor, leaving only C2 (1 uF/6.3 V) plus a 0.1 uF ceramic; this raises input ripple and may starve the boost stage during display-refresh bursts.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build appears to reproduce the historical DC-jack wiring fault (J4 pin 2 tied to BAT+ instead of GND, so the normally-closed 2-3 contact shorts the battery), and C1's value/rating (0.1 uF/16 V) deviate from the spec's intended 1 uF/25 V on the EPD power rail."
}

